  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY NIGHT THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 333 AM CDT Tue Jul 28 2026\n\nHigh pressure remains over the Mid Mississippi Valley on Thursday, \nand then drifts east Thursday night into Friday. Meanwhile, an upper \nlevel short wave moves into the Midwest Thursday into Thursday \nnight.  The wave deepens into a closed low over southern Minnesota \nby 12Z Friday.  The low moves slowly southeast across the \nMississippi Valley through the weekend, finally stalling over \nwestern Kentucky or far southeast Missouri Sunday evening.  The \ndeterministic GFS and ECMWF are in good agreement with the speed and \ntrack low through this period, and both produce periods of precip \nFriday through Sunday.  Clouds and periods of rain associated with \nthe low leads to below normal temperatures in most locations through \nMonday.  Guidance diverges on the position of the cut off low aloft \nby late Monday into Tuesday with the GFS showing it almost directly \nover St. Louis by 18Z Tuesday and the ECMWF putting it over \nnorthwest Tennessee.  While there are differences in strength and \nposition of the low apparent in the deterministic guidance Friday \nthrough Tuesday, the 4 LREF clusters show a very similar synoptic \npattern through the period.  This leads to relatively high \nconfidence in precipitation chances for Friday and Saturday as the \nlow passes across the area.  Individual high temperatures are \nsomewhat less certain Friday through Tuesday, and will ultimately \ndepend on cloud cover and duration of precip each day. This is \nillustrated by 5-8 degree interquartile high temperature ranges each \nday, though even the 75th percentile is below normal.",
